## Command: preserve-mode-behavior
**Purpose**: Ensure changes don't break behavior across different modes/contexts

**When to use**: Any UI/layout/behavioral changes

**Checklist**:
```
If applicable, verify:
- [ ] Mobile behavior intact
- [ ] Tablet behavior intact
- [ ] Desktop behavior intact
- [ ] Other contexts/routes intact
- [ ] No visual/layout breaks
- [ ] All interactive elements work
```

---

## Command: minimal-change-only
**Purpose**: Make only necessary changes, nothing more

**Rules**:
- Change ONLY what's requested
- Don't refactor unrelated code
- Don't "improve" things not asked
- Don't add features not requested
- Don't change variable names unless needed
- Preserve all existing patterns

---

## Command: verify-before-finalize
**Purpose**: Final verification before completing changes

**Checklist**:
- [ ] Matches user's exact request
- [ ] No existing functionality broken
- [ ] All applicable modes/contexts work
- [ ] Layouts/designs preserved
- [ ] No errors (linting, compilation, runtime)
- [ ] Changes are minimal
- [ ] Code follows existing patterns
- [ ] Dependencies considered

---

## Command: understand-first
**Purpose**: Deep understanding before any action

**When to use**: For every user request

**Process**:
1. Parse prompt completely
2. Extract primary request
3. Extract constraints
4. Extract mode/scope specificity
5. Read relevant files
6. Understand current implementation
7. Plan approach
8. Confirm understanding OR ask ONE specific question
9. Execute



